{"step_index":91,"source":"MODEL","type":"PLANNER_RESPONSE","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-10-13T03:14:21Z","input_tokens":67381,"cache_read_tokens":0,"output_tokens":1439,"thinking":"Planning to implement the chosen \"Opsi 1,\" focusing on the interactive mission success modal. The initial step involves handling the API response from the designated progress route. I will examine the existing code in the specified route file to understand how the response data is currently structured.\n\n\nThe route's response currently includes earned badges, but it needs to differentiate *newly* earned badges for targeted celebration. By fetching existing badges before upserting, the newly earned badges can be computed. Verification confirms the presence of `earnedAt` in the database schema. The next step is determining the sound preference from the database to enable celebratory sound effects.\n\n\nA lightweight, dependable sound effect will be implemented using the Web Audio API for victory fanfares. Investigating confetti animation options, a decision will be made between an existing library and a custom Canvas implementation. The \"soundOn\" preference will be checked, either through a passed-down prop or via an in-header toggle with persisted state.\n\nVictory modal details will include dynamic star displays, score earned, block usage comparison, and new badge presentation. Navigation buttons will enable proceeding to the next mission, replaying the current mission, or returning to the map. The badge collection will be incorporated into the map view.\n\n\n","tool_calls":[{"name":"view_file","args":{"AbsolutePath":"\"e:\\\\codekids\\\\src\\\\app\\\\misi\\\\[id]\\\\page.tsx\"","toolAction":"\"Viewing misi page\"","toolSummary":"\"View app/misi/[id]/page.tsx\""}}]}
