{"step_index":101,"source":"MODEL","type":"PLANNER_RESPONSE","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-10-13T03:15:08Z","input_tokens":4027,"cache_read_tokens":73289,"output_tokens":2820,"thinking":"The animation frames are being executed, and the result is handled upon completion. This involves updating the UI with the run result and incrementing the attempt counter. Subsequently, the attempt data, including mission ID, is prepared for submission to a server-side API. The submission is then attempted, and the UI is updated to reflect the submission status.\n\n\nChecking for `window.AudioContext` or its vendor-prefixed variant seems appropriate for sound synthesis. The existence of a saved sound preference in local storage is checked and used to initialize the `enabled` state. The audio context needs to be initialized and resumed when required.\n\n\nAudio playback relies on an oscillator and gain node within the audio context. The `playTone` function configures the oscillator's type, frequency, and gain envelope for sound generation. Victory, star, and badge unlock fanfares are implemented by sequencing individual tones.\n\n\nSound synthesis will be handled using the `AudioContext` and an oscillator, configuring tone frequencies and envelopes for effects. A \"soft click\" uses a sine wave. A victory fanfare is constructed through sequenced tones. The `soundEngine` is designed for standalone, browser-compatible operation with minimal overhead.\n\n\nSound events for star and badge unlocks are triggered at specific timestamps, generating dings and highlighting the earned items visually. UI elements dynamically update based on the mission result, displaying appropriate headlines, star animations, stat pills, and encouragement tips. Navigation buttons are conditionally rendered based on whether a next mission is available.\n\n\nAdding a badge button to the header provides access to a modal displaying the user's unlocked badges and details on locked ones. The badge button and modal components require rendering logic including dynamic content based on unlocked badges. The next step involves checking if sound toggle functionality can be included in the top bars of the `MissionWorkspace` and `PetaPage` components.\n\n\n","tool_calls":[{"name":"view_file","args":{"AbsolutePath":"\"e:\\\\codekids\\\\src\\\\app\\\\api\\\\progress\\\\route.ts\"","EndLine":"137","StartLine":"1","toolAction":"\"Viewing api/progress/route.ts\"","toolSummary":"\"View api/progress/route.ts\""}}]}
{"step_index":102,"source":"MODEL","type":"GENERIC","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-10-13T03:15:28Z","content":"Created At: 2026-10-13T10:15:28+07:00\nCompleted At: 2026-10-13T10:15:28+07:00\nFile Path: `file:///e:/codekids/src/app/api/progress/route.ts`\nTotal Lines: 137\nTotal Bytes: 4407\nShowing lines 1 to 137\nThe following code has been modified to include a line number before every line, in the format: <line_number>: <original_line>. Please note that any changes targeting the original code should remove the line number, colon, and leading space.\n1: import { requireChild } from \"@/lib/session\";\n2: import { db } from \"@/lib/db\";\n3: import { NextResponse } from \"next/server\";\n4: import { getMission, nextMission } from \"@/content/missions\";\n5: import { computeStars, computeScore, evaluateBadges } from \"@/lib/missions/gamification\";\n6: \n7: export async function POST(request: Request) {\n8:   try {\n9:     const child = await requireChild();\n10:     const fd = await request.formData();\n11:     const missionId = fd.get(\"missionId\") as string;\n12:     const success = fd.get(\"success\") === \"true\";\n13:     const blocksUsed = parseInt(fd.get(\"blocksUsed\") as string) || 0;\n14:     const hintsUsed = parseInt(fd.get(\"hintsUsed\") as string) || 0;\n15:     const durationSec = 10; // Demo: should come from client tracking\n16: \n17:     const mission = getMission(missionId);\n18:     if (!mission) return NextResponse.json({ error: \"Mission not found\" }, { status: 404 });\n19: \n20:     // 1. Log Attempt\n21:     await db.attempt.create({\n22:       data: {\n23:         childId: child.id,\n24:         missionId,\n25:         success,\n26:         blocksUsed,\n27:         hintsUsed,\n28:         durationSec,\n29:       }\n30:     });\n31: \n32:     // 2. Fetch past attempts & progress to calculate stats\n33:     const pastAttempts = await db.attempt.findMany({\n34:       where: { childId: child.id, missionId },\n35:       orderBy: { createdAt: \"asc\" }\n36:     });\n37:     const failedAttempts = pastAttempts.filter(a => !a.success).length;\n38:     // maxHintLevel logic will be extracted from ChatLog if Bibi is used\n39:     const maxHintLevel = 0; \n40: \n41:     // 3\n<truncated 1412 bytes>\n:       });\n77:       if (latestAttempt) {\n78:         await db.attempt.update({\n79:           where: { id: latestAttempt.id },\n80:           data: { stars, score }\n81:         });\n82:       }\n83: \n84:       // Check Badges\n85:       const allProgress = await db.progress.findMany({ where: { childId: child.id } });\n86:       const earnedBadges = evaluateBadges(allProgress, { success, stars, hintsUsed });\n87:       for (const badgeId of earnedBadges) {\n88:         await db.childBadge.upsert({\n89:           where: { childId_badgeId: { childId: child.id, badgeId } },\n90:           create: { childId: child.id, badgeId },\n91:           update: {} // do nothing if exists\n92:         });\n93:       }\n94: \n95:       // Update child lastActiveAt\n96:       await db.childProfile.update({\n97:         where: { id: child.id },\n98:         data: { lastActiveAt: new Date() }\n99:       });\n100: \n101:       const next = nextMission(missionId);\n102:       return NextResponse.json({ \n103:         success: true, \n104:         stars, \n105:         score,\n106:         badges: earnedBadges,\n107:         nextMission: next?.id \n108:       });\n109: \n110:     } else {\n111:       // Just update attempts count\n112:       p = await db.progress.upsert({\n113:         where: { childId_missionId: { childId: child.id, missionId } },\n114:         update: { attempts: (p?.attempts || 0) + 1 },\n115:         create: {\n116:           childId: child.id,\n117:           missionId,\n118:           attempts: 1,\n119:           hintsUsed,\n120:         }\n121:       });\n122:       \n123:       // Update child lastActiveAt\n124:       await db.childProfile.update({\n125:         where: { id: child.id },\n126:         da